comment.narrative:
•238 complaints were processed across the KNCHR regions;
•131 of those complaints were by males complainants while 99 were by females and 7 related to intersex persons;
•Ten complaints (4.2%) of the total complaints received were by or relating to rights of PWDs;
•3 Strategic partners engagement forums held with partners in Mombasa, Wajir and Bomet and complaints processing partnership strengthened with 18 partners;
•Three (3) Joint public complaints handling initiatives held in  Maralal, Moyale and Homabay;
•At least 293 members of the public sensitized on human rights complaints processing;
•63 complaints received and processed towards resolution.
•Seven (7) complaints handling officers debriefed and taken through mental health awareness.

•16 Pro-bono advocates trained on litigation of HRs cases and HRBA approach in litigation towards establishing a consortium of pro-bono lawyers;
•Engagement with the CUC in Narok and  establishment of a new partnership with CUC in West Pokot; 
•47 CUC members were sensitized on HRBA, handling of SGBV cases, ADR mechanisms and access to justice for petty offenders;
•Eighty eight (88) SGBV survivors of the 2007 General Elections (Kisumu, Kakamega & Vihiga) offered psycho-social support, and their resilience and social skills enhanced.

•Three trial observations conducted in Nyahururu Murder. Case . 7 of 2020, MKS Crimn Case No.1229 of 2018 and Inquest No 2 of 2017 in Isiolo ;
•Advisories rendered to Court on infusion of HRs principles.
•One (1) report on monitoring County Laws on disabilities/PWDs rights finalized.
